# Architecture (MANDATORY)

This is a **MODULAR MONOLITH**. Never introduce microservices.

## Layering (strict)

```
route/page  →  service  →  repository  →  prisma
```

- `prisma` may ONLY be imported in `src/modules/*/repository/*.ts` and `src/shared/db/prisma.ts`. Never in routes, services, components, or utils.
- Modules communicate ONLY through each other's `index.ts`. Never import another module's internal folders.
- Never write cross-module Prisma joins. Compose in the service layer.

## Module layout

```
src/modules/<name>/
  domain/       pure business logic, types — no I/O, prisma, or fetch
  repository/   all prisma access for this module
  service/      use-cases, transactions, calls repositories
  index.ts      public API — ONLY file other modules may import
```

Existing: inventory, rates, booking, payment, ledger, guest, catalog, invoice, integration, channel, staff, feedback, outbox  

Channel / OTA: foundation + adapter stubs live in `src/modules/channel`.  
Real OpenTravel/partner HTTP stays inside adapters only — never in routes/services/repos.
